  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed Road map &amp; variety testing Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen Indonesia&#x2019;s horticultural sector by establishing a robust seed enabling environment that supports transparent and professional regulatory services. Through targeted capacity-building, government experts are equipped to implement high-quality seed regulation across the value chain. In parallel, new vegetable and potato varieties have been successfully tested at two locations in Indonesia and are now ready for uptake by Indonesian growers.-	Enabling environment that facilitates transparent and professional seed regulatory services;-	Government experts capacitated in implementing quality seed regulatory services; and-	New varieties of vegetables and potato successfully tested at two locations in Indonesia, ready for uptake by Indonesian growers.</narrative>
  </description>
